 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Authorizes the empire state development corporation to develop a public awareness campaign promoting businesses located in New York state with an emphasis on small businesses and the need to shop in downtown local areas; requires the creation of the Buy New York Online Networking Directory to connect purchasers with businesses located in New York.",
 "title": "Authorizes the empire state development corporation to develop a public awareness campaign promoting businesses located in New York state",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A8932",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A8932-2021",
     "printNo": "A8932",
     "session": 2021,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 151\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 8932, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  authorizing  the  empire  state development corporation to\n      develop a public awareness campaign promoting  businesses  located\n      in New York state\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  legislation  would  require  Empire  State  Development (ESD) to\nestablish and implement a public awareness campaign including a  website\npromoting  businesses located in New York State and encouraging individ-\nuals and businesses to purchase products and services  from  such  busi-\nnesses.\n \n  In  order to carry out this new mandate, ESD would need to engage in a\npaid media and strategy campaign to gauge effectiveness  of  the  legis-\nlation  as  well as to create a new database of businesses, which can be\nduplicative of other sources. The bill carries no appropriation for  ESD\nto implement this new mandate.\n \n  Historically,   ESD   has  carried  out  successful  public  awareness\ncampaigns to promote New York as a premiere tourism destination, encour-\nage businesses to locate and expand in New York, and to promote food and\nbeverages grown and developed in-State. These campaigns have been  based\non  market  data,  carefully  targeted, and narrowly messaged to achieve\ntheir goals. The type of campaign outlined in the  proposed  legislation\nfundamentally diverges from those prior campaigns.\n \n  For these reasons, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 151,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2022
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
